# Icechunk fixture repos are GENERATED (Blade.IcechunkWrite, at test time) --
# nothing in here is committed but this file, the README beside it, and the
# ONE exception below.
#
# The zarr_stores/ precedent is why this exists from day one: that directory's
# README says nothing is committed, yet 161 generated files are tracked,
# because there was no .gitignore to enforce the claim.
#
# THE EXCEPTION: golden_py/ is committed on purpose. It is the only repo here
# that Blade did not write -- icechunk-python 2.1.2 did -- so it cannot be
# regenerated by the test run the way every other fixture is, and a reader that
# only ever meets bytes its own twin wrote is not being tested against the
# FORMAT. `make_golden_py.py` beside it is its provenance; it is run by hand,
# never by the build or the suite. See the README.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!make_golden_py.py
# The directory has to be un-ignored before git will descend into it, and the
# `*` above re-excludes everything inside once it does -- hence both lines.
!golden_py/
!golden_py/**
